# Array Operator — arrayoperator.com (Netlify static + Railway API proxy)
# Mirrors the NEPOOL Operator (nepooloperator.com) proxy pattern so the whole
# owner flow is SAME-ORIGIN and branded: the static marketing/onboarding pages
# are served by Netlify, while /v1/* (API), /accounts (dashboard SPA), and the
# onboarding SPA proxy through to the shared FastAPI backend on Railway.

# ── Backend API (Railway) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# onboarding.html + app.js call the API at the same origin via /v1/* once
# API_BASE = "" (relative). Proxy them to Railway so they work from
# arrayoperator.com. (Stripe webhooks + the Chrome extension hit Railway directly.)
/v1/*                 https://web-production-49c83.up.railway.app/v1/:splat   200

# ── Account dashboard SPA (served at /app/* on Railway) ─────────────────
# Status-200 proxy so the address bar shows arrayoperator.com/accounts.
# The SPA is built with base/basename = /accounts so assets + routing resolve.
/accounts             https://web-production-49c83.up.railway.app/app/   200
/accounts/*           https://web-production-49c83.up.railway.app/app/:splat   200

# ── Phone app (React owner-web, served at /m) ───────────────────────────
# The dedicated phone client is a static Vite build in public/m/ (regenerate
# with: cd apps/owner-web && vite build --base=/m/ → copy dist/* to public/m/).
# Its client-side routes (/m/fleet, /m/invoices, …) have no backing file, so
# fall back to the app shell. Real assets (/m/assets/*) exist on disk and are
# served directly — Netlify only applies this rewrite when no file matches.
/m/*                  /m/index.html      200

# ── Pretty onboarding URL ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The landing-page Array door links to arrayoperator.com/onboarding (no .html).
# Serve the static onboarding wizard from the clean URL. The wizard calls the
# API via the same-origin /v1/* proxy above, so no extra API rule is needed.
/onboarding           /onboarding.html   200
/signup               /onboarding.html   301
/get-started          /onboarding.html   301

# ── Pretty login URL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Inline email+password sign-in (also exchanges a magic-link ?token=). Calls
# the same-origin /v1/* proxy above. The EnergyAgent landing page's "Log in to
# Array Operator" button points here.
/login                /login.html        200
/signin               /login.html        301

# ── Offtaker invoice pay return (Stripe Checkout) ───────────────────────
# After an offtaker pays (or cancels), Stripe sends them here — a PUBLIC
# thank-you page with NO owner SPA and NO session. Never / or /#reports.
/paid                 /paid.html         200
/paid.html            /paid.html         200
